{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> One may say: after they sinned and the decree of death was decreed upon them, they were told 'be fruitful and multiply,' because they now needed [the commandment of] procreation, since it says <b>and fill the earth</b> — for had this been said about them before they sinned, it should have written 'and fill the garden,' since their dwelling was there before they sinned. Rather, because procreation is similar to creation, it was written here together with the act of creation." "<b>And subdue it.</b> Raphe (without dagesh), for it is in the language of a command; but had it been with a dagesh, it would be understood as past tense, like <b>קבצו</b> (Jeremiah 3:17 — 'they shall gather'), with pataḥ."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:20:09.175605509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}